# ==============================================================================
# IRIS — Silksong Mobile Modding Ecosystem Build & Packaging Script (IRIS v2.9.6)
#
# Changes in IRIS v2.9.6:
# - Fixed Auric Aegis (`AstrumNova-AuricAegis-1.1.2`) Infinite Stagger & Never-Ending Boss Fight:
#   * Moved `IsFinalJudgeFsmStateEnter` from `MethodHookChain` (which blocked the entire shared `FsmState::OnEnter()`
#     chain `chainId=111` across all scenes except `Coral_Judge_Arena` whenever `FinalJudge` was installed) onto
#     per-patch `PatchMethodMetadata` inside `CanInvokePatchForInstanceAndResult`. Now `PrimedSentinel.OnFSMStateEntered`
#     executes properly in `Hang_17b` to reset `stunCounter = 0`, destroy `"Stun Control"`, and enter Phase 2.
#   * Added `HarmonyBridge.AuricAegis_PreFsmEnabled`, `AuricAegis_PostFsmStateEntered`, `AuricAegis_CanContinueCoroutine`,
#     and `AuricAegis_OnDeathReset` + Cecil IL injection for `Silksong.Mods.PrimedSentinel.PrimedSentinel`:
#     - Cleans stale static `control` / `enable` / `phase2` state on scene transitions or repeat runs.
#     - Restores `healthManager.hp = INITIAL_HP` (`1800`) on `"Battle Start"` if `Pantheon of Pharloom` scaled HP to `2908`,
#       preventing a 14-stagger Phase 1 loop before `PHASE_2_THRESHOLD` (`1500`).
#     - Explicitly clears `healthManager.IsInvincible = false`, disables `"Stun Control"`, and nulls `healthManager.stunControlFsm`
#       when transitioning to Phase 2 (`hp <= PHASE_2_THRESHOLD`).
#     - Guards all `PrimedSentinel` coroutines (`ForceNextState`, `scheduleNextState`, `FixRisingSlash`, `diveTurnAround`,
#       `delayedTurnAround`, `disableInvincibility`) so they abort immediately when `healthManager.isDead || healthManager.hp <= 0`,
#       preventing pending state-transition coroutines from yanking `Song Knight` out of its `"ZERO HP"` defeat sequence.
#   * Bridged `HeroController::reaperModeEffect` field loads/stores (`GetHeroReaperModeEffect` / `SetHeroReaperModeEffect`)
#     to eliminate `MissingFieldException: field HeroController::reaperModeEffect not exists` in `ModLog.log`.
# - Rebranded API to `IRIS` (`IRIS v2.9.6`) & Implemented Stealth Cinema Ribbon Loading Screen:
#   * Replaced `ModPreloaderScreen` with the flat dark **Stealth Cinema Ribbon** UI (`#060608` backdrop, `#0D0D11` top & bottom
#     letterbox strips with `#22222C` 1px borders, 3px solid `#ECECEF` edge-to-edge progress line, zero gradients).
#   * Displays `IRIS` in the center space alongside 40 unique Silksong/gaming messages (10 user messages + 30 custom messages,
#     no leading numbers), advancing to a new random message each time a loading procedure step completes.
# - Hid Blocked Mods & Removed Stitchwork / PatchWork UI References:
#   * Removed all `Stitchwork` and `Patchwork` buttons, skin pack indicators, circular bubble entries, and loading overlays from UI.
#   * Filtered out all incompatible/blocked mods from `InstalledMods`, `OnlineCatalog`, and `_discoveredConfigs` so blocked mods
#     are never shown anywhere in the UI.
# - Added Full `Profile` System (`BepInEx/config/iris_profile.jsonc`):
#   * Added `Profile` tab to the in-game console (`_uGuiModConsolePanelGo` & IMGUI fallback) with editable Profile Name,
#     live sync status (`MODS SYNCED WITH PROFILE` vs `Mods not synced with profile`), native Android File Manager
#     Import & Export (`NativeFilePicker.PickFile` / `ExportFile` + fallback), and `Missing X mods from the profile — do you want
#     to download them?` with a 3-second hold-to-download button featuring a smooth filling animation that downloads all
#     missing mods and their transitive dependencies.
#
# Changes in v2.9.5:
# - Removed & Blocked `Stitchwork` and `StitchworkWiki` While Preserving Stitchwork Skins:
#   * Added `Stitchwork`, `SilksongSkinCreators-Stitchwork`, `StitchworkWiki`, and `SilksongSkinCreators-StitchworkWiki` to `_excludedArchitectOrPortingNames` (`IsExcludedModIdentifier`), while exempting Stitchwork skin/voice packs (`IsStitchworkSkinOrAssetPackName`).
#   * Updated `InGameModMenu.IsArchitectOrDependentPackage` and `IsBuiltInOrNativeMobileDependency` so `Stitchwork` and `StitchworkWiki` are removed from the online catalog and installed mods list, while skin/voice packs that list `Stitchwork` in their `dependencies` (`064_Teto_Voice_for_Stitchwork`, `069_VoidHornet`, etc.) remain in the catalog and stage their assets into `PatchWork/` without downloading `Stitchwork`.
#   * Hardened `PreOrganizeTopLevelPcModDlls()` and `DiscoverCandidatesInRoot()` to automatically disable `Stitchwork.dll` and `StitchworkWiki.dll` (`.disabled`) and refuse to load them even if manually placed in `BepInEx/plugins/` or `BepInEx/pc_mods/`.
# - Audited & Bridged All 90 Mods Across `Silksong_Mods_Batch_02.zip` (`059`–`086`) and `Silksong_Mods_Batch_03.zip` (`087`–`151`):
#   * `059_SilkGoddess`, `061_SteelMaskTint`, `064_Teto_Voice_for_Stitchwork`, `069_VoidHornet`, `124_CustomDifficulty`: Extended `StagePatchworkAndCustomizerAssetPacks()` to stage `Patchworks/` (plural) and `Stitchwork/` skin/audio packs into `BepInEx/plugins/PatchWork/`, and added `NormalizeBackslashExtractedFiles()` to fix Windows backslash ZIP entries (`124_CustomDifficulty`).
#   * `059_SilkGoddess` & `087_AnySilkBoss`: Rewrote `SilkGoddess.AssetManager` and `AnySilkBoss.Source.Managers.AssetManager` platform bundle folder fallback to `"Android"`, preserved `"scenes_scenes_scenes/"` relative paths in `AssetHelperBridge.ResolveAndroidBundlePath()`, enabled `GameManager::BeginSceneTransition` hook chaining for all mods in `ShouldSkipProblematicNativeHook()`, and added `FadeNestedFadeGroup` / `NestedFadeGroupTimedFader` shims (`081_AltCrests`, `087_AnySilkBoss`).
