# Changelog (v2.9.2):
# - Fixed Bonemaster Ground Trap ("Bite Jaw" / `ant_traps`) "Two White Lines" Sprite Glitch (Test 11 `2026-11-17_12-33-52/ModLog.log:183`):
#   * Root Cause 1 (`ResourceLocationMap.Locate` Type Filter in `lib/Unity.Addressables.dll` `rva=0x77d0`):
#     - Disassembly of `ResourceLocationMap.Locate(object key, Type type, out IList<IResourceLocation> locations)` confirmed that passing `typeof(IAssetBundleResource)` returns `false` whenever `catalogKey` has `ResourceType == typeof(SpriteAtlas)` or `typeof(Sprite)` (where the `IAssetBundleResource` is in `loc.Dependencies`), causing 1/61 `Borrow.wants` (`"ant_traps"` / `"ant_traps.spriteatlas"`) to miss at the loading screen (`Preloaded 60/61 BossKit Borrow wants`).
#     - Updated `CoOpenAndPreloadAllBossKitBorrowWants` to call `locator.Locate(catalogKey, null, out var locs)` and collect both direct `IAssetBundleResource` locations and all `IAssetBundleResource` dependencies in `loc.Dependencies`, plus added `"spriteatlases_assets_all"` and `"textures_assets_areaant"` to `requestedBundles` and matched singular `"ant_trap"` in `BonemasterCatalogKeyIndexOf`.
#   * Root Cause 2 (`TryLoadFromIndexedBundles` CAB-Hash Bundle Name Check & `IndexAssetBundlePaths` Atlas Extraction):
#     - Removed the `bn.IndexOf("ant_traps") >= 0` check in `TryLoadFromIndexedBundles` (Addressables `AssetBundle.name` is a 32-char hex CAB hash, never `"ant_traps"`), and updated `IndexAssetBundlePaths` to immediately load `SpriteAtlas` and `ant_trap*` `Sprite` assets into `_bmSpriteCache` and `_addressableAssetCache["ant_traps"]` when indexing any bundle containing `ant_trap` or `.spriteatlas` paths.
#   * Root Cause 3 (`BonemasterPicturesFind` Premature Fallback to `GetOrCreateFallbackBoneSpikeSprite()` & `BonemasterSpritePropShow` Collider Update):
#     - Moved `TryLoadFromIndexedBundles(name, typeof(Sprite))` and `ResolveAddressableAsset(name, typeof(Sprite))` ahead of the fallback in `BonemasterPicturesFind`, replaced the static white-line fallback with a multi-frame jagged bone-jaw procedural sprite fallback (`GetOrCreateProceduralAntTrapSprite`), and updated `BonemasterSpritePropShow` so `ShowTell()` (`antic` frames) does not block `Grow()` from updating `PolygonCollider2D` to the full spike jaw outline.
# - Fixed Bonemaster Parry Brown Screen Effect (`BoneCounter.Mud` -> `Blind.InHerFace` -> `LensCloud.Throw`):
#   * Previously `BossKit.Fight.LensCloud::Throw` was stubbed to `ldnull; ret;` in `CecilEngine.cs` because `LensCloud.Build`/`LateUpdate` called UnityLinker-stripped `ParticleSystem.EmitParams` and `ParticleSystem.Particle` setters (`ModLog.log:163-204`).
#   * Added `AssetHelperBridge.BonemasterLensCloudThrow`, `BonemasterLensCloudClearAll`, and `BonemasterLensCloudBehaviour : MonoBehaviour` rendering the 4-layer camera-parented brown screen blind effect (umber flinch flash, maggot/speckle grime vignette, soft radial veil, and counter-swirling sinking dirt puff clouds) using `SpriteRenderer`s with zero stripped `ParticleSystem` setters, and redirected `LensCloud::Throw` and `LensCloud::ClearAll` in `CecilEngine.cs`.
# - Added `HkCore` (`v2.0`) & `SsBossLoader` (`v1.0`) Compatibility Bridges:
#   * Added `PatchProcessor.ReadMethodBody` overloads in `BepInExShims.cs` and stubbed `HkCore.PlayerDataOverlay::RedirectHkFieldUsers` in `CecilEngine.cs` (preventing IL body reads on IL2CPP `Assembly-CSharp` methods).
#   * Rewrote `SystemInfo.get_graphicsDeviceType` inside `HkCore.HkScenes/<LoadShaders>d__63::MoveNext` to `21` (`GraphicsDeviceType.Vulkan`) so Android `OpenGLES3` devices load `hk_shaders_glvk.bundle` (`"glvk"`), and prioritized `HkCore` (`5`) before `SsBossLoader` (`50`) in `GetModDependencyPriority`.
