# Changelog (v2.9.0):
# - Fixed Test 9 (`2026-11-17_10-07-48.zip`) `Bonemaster` (`Kiahah-Bonemaster-1.0.6`) corpse not spawning in `Ant_Queen` & boss not spawning in `Memory_Ant_Queen`, verified against `ModLog.log`, `LogOutput.log`, `Original_PC_Mod/Bonemaster.dll`, and `lib/mscorlib.dll`:
#   * Root Cause 1 (`ModLog.log:332-337` — `System.TypeLoadException: Could not load type 'System.ValueTuple`6' from assembly 'mscorlib'` during `ScanAndLoadPCMods`):
#     - On the Android device's stripped IL2CPP `mscorlib.dll`, UnityLinker stripped `System.ValueTuple`5`, `System.ValueTuple`6`, `System.ValueTuple`7`, and `System.ValueTuple`8` (only `ValueTuple` and `ValueTuple`1`..`4` exist in `mscorlib.dll` at runtime).
#     - In `CecilEngine.VerifyAndAutoShimTypeReferences`, `rootTref.Name.StartsWith("ValueTuple")` was unconditionally redirecting ALL `ValueTuple` arities (including `ValueTuple`5` and `ValueTuple`6`) to `mscorlib`, causing `AppDomain.CurrentDomain.Load(bytes)` to throw `TypeLoadException: Could not load type 'System.ValueTuple`6' from assembly 'mscorlib'` so `Bonemaster.dll` never loaded (`Loaded PC Mods` in `ModLog.log:11` omitted `Bonemaster`).
#     - Fixed `VerifyAndAutoShimTypeReferences` to redirect `System.ValueTuple*` to `mscorlib` ONLY when `typeof(object).Assembly.GetType(tref.FullName.Replace('/', '+'), false) != null`, allowing missing 5+-arity `ValueTuple`s to be synthesized in `SilksongMobileAPI_AutoShims_<modName>` AND skipping the `allMemberRefs` parameter-clobbering loop on synthesized `ValueTuple`s so `.ctor(!0..!N)` signatures are never mutated to `System.Object`.
#   * Root Cause 2 (`Original_PC_Mod/Bonemaster.dll` `ValueTuple`5` & `ValueTuple`6` IL2CPP AOT Generic Container Neutralization):
#     - Exhaustive metadata scan of `Bonemaster.dll` confirmed that `TypeRef[282]` (`System.ValueTuple`5`) and `TypeRef[411]` (`System.ValueTuple`6`) are used in only two places: `BossKit.Fight.SpriteProp::turning` (`FIELD[840]`, `Nullable<ValueTuple`5<float, float, float, Func<float, float>, float>>`) and `Bonemaster.Boss.ImpactFrame/<>c__DisplayClass34_0::rims` (`FIELD[1954]`, `List<ValueTuple`6<Transform, Transform, Vector3, MeshRenderer, Material, Material>>`).
#     - Rewrote `BossKit.Fight.SpriteProp` (`turns` and `turning` fields -> `System.Object`, `Turn` -> `AssetHelperBridge.BonemasterSpritePropTurn`, `Update` turn step `IL_01b7..IL_0292` -> `AssetHelperBridge.BonemasterSpritePropStepTurn`) and stubbed `Bonemaster.Boss.ImpactFrame` (`Begin` -> `false`, `Blow`/`End`/`CatchBones`/`Dark`/`Light`/`White` -> `ret`, `<>c__DisplayClass34_0` fields -> `System.Object`) so `Bonemaster.dll` never instantiates `Nullable<ValueTuple`5>` or `List<ValueTuple`6>` on Android IL2CPP ARM64.
#   * Root Cause 3 (`Bonemaster.World.Corpse` `defeatedAntQueen` Gate & `CoEnsureBonemasterShelfPreloaded` Early-Return Fix):
#     - In `Bonemaster.World.Corpse/<Lay>d__25::MoveNext` (`rva=0x2c81c`), `Corpse.Lay(scene)` checked `PlayerData.instance.GetBool("defeatedAntQueen")` before calling `Corpse.Body(scene)`, `Corpse.Entry(scene, val)`, and `Message.Lay(scene, 35f, 20f)`, and `Corpse.Entry` (`rva=0x2c464`) checked `PlayerData.instance.GetBool("hasNeedolinMemoryPowerup")`. Patched both checks in `CecilEngine` to `true` (`pop; ldc.i4.1`) so the corpse, Needolin memory entry, and lore message always spawn in `Ant_Queen`.
#     - Fixed `CoEnsureBonemasterShelfPreloaded` so when `_bonemasterShelfPreloaded` was already set at `Menu_Title`, entering `Ant_Queen` (`!forcePreload`) still runs the `Ant_Queen` corpse/entry verification fallback instead of returning early at line 1, and invokes `Shelf.Hold(bareBmScene)` before loading `Ant_04` so its dependency AssetBundles remain pinned across scene transitions.
#   * Log Noise Filter (`ModLog.log:385-520`):
#     - Filtered benign `Could not load crest ` Unity errors in `HandleUnityLog` / `OnUnityLogMessageReceived` when a save slot references an uninstalled custom crest (e.g., `Weaver_Codex`).
# Changelog (v2.9.0):
# - Fixed Test 8 (`test8.zip` & `2026-11-17_08-35-49.zip`) `Bonemaster` (`Kiahah-Bonemaster-1.0.6`) & loading-screen crashes verified against `lib/Assembly-CSharp.dll`, `lib/AssetHelper.dll`, `lib/mscorlib.dll`, and `Original_PC_Mod/Bonemaster.dll`:
#   * Post-Preloader Native Crash Fix (`ModPreloaderScreen.RunPreloader` in `Logs/2026-11-17_07-11-28/LogOutput.log:771-772` & `07-47-37/LogOutput.log:973-974`):
#     - Removed `Modding.PlayMakerPrefabPreprocessor.PreprocessAllModPrefabFsms()` and `Resources.UnloadUnusedAssets()` from `ModPreloaderScreen.RunPreloader()`.
#     - In Unity, `DontDestroyOnLoad` is a valid loaded scene (`sc.IsValid() && sc.isLoaded`), so `PreprocessAllModPrefabFsms()` (`!sc.IsValid() || !sc.isLoaded`) was calling `fsm.Preprocess()` on 666 uninstantiated raw AssetBundle prefab assets in memory (`localpoolprefabs_assets_areaant`, etc.) and then immediately calling `Resources.UnloadUnusedAssets()`, unloading sub-assets of those 666 mutated prefabs and crashing 1 second after preloader completion.
#   * `Pre_Menu_Intro` Premature Additive Load & 39.7s Scene-Transition Stall Fix (`08-35-49/LogOutput.log:945-971`):
#     - Updated `IsSafeSceneForBatchExtraction(string sceneName)` to return `true` ONLY on `"Menu_Title"` (never `"Pre_Menu_Intro"`).
#     - Fixed `ModPreloaderScreen.RunPreloader()` `waitMenu` condition to wait explicitly for `"Menu_Title"` (previously `!string.Equals(sc.name, "Pre_Menu_Intro") && !sc.name.StartsWith("Init")` broke on frame 1 while the boot scene was still active before `Pre_Menu_Intro`).
#     - Unified `CoRunCoalescedSceneExtractions()` with `RunPreloaderPharloomsGloryBatchExtract()` under `_pharloomsGloryBatchRunning` so two `RunPharloomsGloryBatchExtractCoroutine` instances never race across the `Pre_Menu_Intro` -> `Menu_Title` `LoadSceneMode.Single` transition.
#   * `Bonemaster` IL2CPP `ValueTuple` Static Constructor (`.cctor`) & Method Neutralization (`Original_PC_Mod/Bonemaster.dll` disassembly):
#     - Stubbed `.cctor` (`Ret`) on `BossKit.World.Words` (`rva=0x79da`), `BossKit.Fight.Machines` (`rva=0xb430`), `BossKit.Fight.Title` (`rva=0x1792c`), `BossKit.Core.Recolour` (`rva=0x2330c`), `BossKit.Core.Shake` (`rva=0x243e9`), `BossKit.Core.DrawingCrop` (`rva=0x1a618`), and `BossKit.Fight.SharpDrawing` (`rva=0x11882`) so none of those 7 static constructors instantiate `new Dictionary<ValueTuple<...>, ...>()` (which triggers AOT `ExecutionEngineException` inside `EqualityComparer<ValueTuple<...>>.get_Default()` on Android IL2CPP ARM64).
#     - Added `AssetHelperBridge.BonemasterShakeShortened`, `BonemasterMachinesOnHit`, `BonemasterMachinesOnHitPrefix`, and `BonemasterTitleShowBig`, and stubbed `BossKit.World.Borrow::IndexFiles()` (`rva=0x3a04`).
#     - Fixed `CoEnsureBonemasterShelfPreloaded` to clone `"Bone Hunter"` onto `Shelf.ShelfRoot` BEFORE deactivating `Ant_04` roots, keep `clone.SetActive(true)` on the inactive `ShelfRoot` (matching `Shelf.Take` `rva=0x71d8` so `Body.Spawn` -> `Shelf.Copy` spawns an active boss), call `RestoreTemplateComponentsEnabled(clone)`, and remove invalid `DontDestroyOnLoad(clone)` on a non-root child object.
#   * Zero-NRE Additive Scene Extraction Guards (`ModLog.log` Section 7):
#     - Added extraction lifecycle guards for `GrassBehaviour::Awake`, `AudioSourceGamePause::Awake`, `EnemyHitEffectsRegular::OnAwake`, `EnemyDeathEffectsRegular::OnAwake`, `PersonalObjectPool::OnStart`, `HealthManager::OnStart`, `TestGameObjectActivator::Start`, `VentRegion::Start`, `HeroTouchForce::Start`, and `GradeMarker::Update` (plus `beh.enabled = false` for `GradeMarker` in `SceneExtractionLifecycleGuard_Prefix`).
#   * Bumped Cecil disk cache directory to `.cecil_cache_v289`.
# Changelog (v2.9.0):
# - Fixed Test 8 `Bonemaster` (`Kiahah-Bonemaster-1.0.6`) instant crash on startup and applied `AeternalEverwatcher` last-priority ordering:
#   * Coroutine Type-Mismatch Fix (`BossKit.World.Borrow.Open`):
#     - In `BossKit.World.Borrow.Open(string bundle)`, original method returns `System.Collections.IEnumerator`.
#     - Cecil rewrite was previously redirecting to `AssetHelperBridge.BonemasterBorrowOpenFast` returning `UnityEngine.AssetBundle`.
#     - When `BossKit.World.Borrow.LoadAll()` executed `yield return Open(text);`, Unity's C++ coroutine manager received an `AssetBundle` object pointer instead of `IEnumerator`, causing an unhandled native abort / SIGABRT at `Menu_Title`.
#     - Updated `AssetHelperBridge.BonemasterBorrowOpenFast` to return `IEnumerator` with `yield break;` and pre-populate `Borrow.opened` with loaded bundles, matching the expected method signature.
#   * Empty Coroutine Provider (`BossKit.Fight.SharpDrawing.FinishLater`):
#     - Updated `FinishLater` rewrite to call `AssetHelperBridge.EmptyCoroutine()` instead of emitting `ldnull; ret;`, preventing `Runner.Run(null)` from throwing `ArgumentNullException` inside `MonoBehaviour.StartCoroutine`.
#   * AeternalEverwatcher Last Priority Configuration:
#     - In `GetModDependencyPriority`: set `AeternalEverwatcher` priority to `1000` (while standard mods are `50`), ensuring it sorts and loads strictly last.
#     - In `HarmonyBridge.ApplySinglePatch`: set `priority = HarmonyLib.Priority.Last` (0) for `AeternalEverwatcher` patches.
